index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0bfe5b9792b2bee86116790d200e835403bcf46a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vla_lab/RECAP.md
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# RECAP on the RB‑Y1 SmolVLA lab
+
+This experiment uses the original RB‑Y1 T1–T10 benchmark, not a replacement
+simulator. It preserves the course evaluation environments, success condition,
+50-action prediction/execution, and public seeds. It adapts the [π*0.6
+RECAP post-training recipe](https://arxiv.org/html/2511.14759v2#S4), not its
+full-scale pre-training. Code readiness, a one-episode smoke, and a learned value
+pass are **not** success-rate results.
+
+## Reproduce the starting policy and diagnose
+
+Follow `docs/VLA_실습_lightwheel_SmolVLA.md` for 50 successful oracle
+demonstrations/task, RB‑Y1 export validation, merged corpus, and stock 25,000-update
+SmolVLA from `lerobot/smolvla_base`. Use the original oracle path for B0, including
+the official recorded terminal row. Set seed 1000 and read `checkpoints/last`.
+Before export, `./run_python.sh vla_lab/scripts/audit_oracle_pngs.py "$RAW_ROOT"`
+checks the 50 raw episodes' camera frame sets, metadata shapes and PNG integrity
+without changing them. The official exporter and validation are still required.
+Run `eval_smolvla.sh --policy-path "$B0" --output "$B0_EVAL" --device cuda:0`
+with all ten tasks/public seeds; then run
+`./run_python.sh vla_lab/scripts/failure_analysis.py --eval "$B0_EVAL"`.
+`./run_python.sh vla_lab/scripts/summarize_recap_b0.py --eval "$B0_EVAL"`
+validates the 500 scores and produces a diagnostic trace shortlist and the
+failure-file digest. Use the actual traces to diagnose one cause and freeze
+`TARGET_STAGE` before the comparative runs. Stage frequencies alone are not
+causal evidence and public traces must not enter training.
+
+Use the same course Python and PyTorch pins. If TorchCodec 0.5+cu128 reports
+`libnppicc.so.12` missing, provision the matching CUDA 12.8 NPP runtime within the
+isolated course environment, not system-wide, and test the decoder first. For all
+training/evaluation stages capture `nvidia-smi` samples with `vram_monitor.py`, wall
+time, counts, exact flags and checkpoint hashes. Do not run a setup/diagnostic
+from a user-specific experiment cache in evaluation.
+
+## Gather genuine experience and fit value
+
+Run from the course repository. `B0`, `ROLLOUTS`, `ORACLE_ROOT`, `MIXED`, `VALUE`,
+`B1_RUN`, `R1_RUN`, `B1_EVAL`, `R1_EVAL` are explicit local paths.
+
+```bash
+for i in $(seq 1 10); do
+  ./vla_lab/collect_recap_rollouts.sh --policy-path "$B0" --task "T$i" \
+    --split train --output "$ROLLOUTS" --device cuda:0
+done
+./run_python.sh vla_lab/scripts/build_recap_mixed.py \
+  --oracle-root "$ORACLE_ROOT" --rollout-root "$ROLLOUTS" --output "$MIXED" \
+  --rollouts-per-task 20
+./run_python.sh vla_lab/scripts/fit_recap_value.py --mixed-root "$MIXED" \
+  --output "$VALUE" --device cuda
+```
+
+Default experience seeds 4000–4019 are disjoint from oracle and public seeds.
+Collector retains whole trajectories (including failures), actual executed
+actions and a separate terminal observation. Never use `--split dev`, public
+episodes or unknown seeds in the training corpus. Keep no more than 100
+train episodes/task including oracle. Verify manifest source identity and fixed
+normalization; preserve logs for any infrastructure retry.
+
+The critic has 201 return bins, uses observable RGB/state/task only, fits
+two folds split by episode, and estimates N=50 advantages without bootstrapping
+at termination. It caches only the active training fold's resized tensors on
+CPU (up to 2048 MiB; `--train-cache-mib 0` disables the cache without changing
+inputs or sampling). Failure penalty C=task horizon and normalization H+C are local
+choices. The oracle first success row is terminal for value and **not** an actor
+target for either matched arm. Require the report to pass its learned-value and
+thresholded-class coverage gates. A failed gate produces no usable labels; it is
+not a valid negative comparison. The initial recipe is autonomous-only (human
+correction and CFG are optional in RECAP and not needed for this variant).
+
+## Pair the actors and evaluate unchanged
+
+```bash
+./run_python.sh vla_lab/scripts/train_recap_actor.py --arm B1 --base "$B0" \
+  --dataset "$MIXED" --output "$B1_RUN"
+./run_python.sh vla_lab/scripts/train_recap_actor.py --arm R1 --base "$B0" \
+  --dataset "$MIXED" --output "$R1_RUN" \
+  --labels "$VALUE/advantage_labels.json" --value-report "$VALUE/value_report.json"
+./vla_lab/eval_smolvla.sh --policy-path "$B1_RUN/deploy/pretrained_model" \
+  --output "$B1_EVAL" --device cuda:0
+./vla_lab/eval_smolvla.sh --policy-path "$R1_RUN/deploy/pretrained_model" \
+  --output "$R1_EVAL" --device cuda:0
+for score in "$B1_EVAL" "$R1_EVAL"; do
+  ./run_python.sh vla_lab/scripts/failure_analysis.py --eval "$score"
+done
+for reference in "$B1_EVAL" "$B0_EVAL"; do
+  ./run_python.sh vla_lab/scripts/recap_compare.py --baseline "$reference" \
+    --candidate "$R1_EVAL" --target-stage "$TARGET_STAGE"
+done
+```
+
+Match seed 1000, 5,000 updates, batch 16, LR 2e-5, warmup 200, same initial policy,
+data, sampling and preprocessing for B1 and R1. R1 supplies its binary advantage
+condition to stock action flow matching with 30% independently seeded condition
+dropout; its saved pipeline selects positive at deployment and needs no training
+labels/value model. The new processor class is available from `vla_lab/scripts`
+via the existing evaluation wrapper. Publish only the selected deploy
+`pretrained_model` and reproduction code when permitted, not `training_state`.
+
+Report R1–B1 (controlled extraction effect) **and** R1–B0 (net baseline change,
+not one-factor causal). Use all 500 fixed pairs, ten-task mean ± sample standard
+deviation, paired 95% interval, failed-stage distribution and wall time/peak VRAM.
+Public evaluation is not a model-selection or repair dataset.
